  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "Tan skin as a proxy for race",
  "description": "The text 'they might just be tan' is mapped onto the visual of the woman with a tan complexion. The meme uses her tan skin as a visual representation of the textual claim that a person's skin color might be due to sun exposure rather than race. This creates an analogical mapping where the woman's tan skin is projected as the 'reason' for the judgment mentioned in the text, deflecting from the serious issue of racial bias.",
